Package: parrot-janitor
Version: @VER@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: Abdellah ERRAOUI <abdellah.erraoui@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-pyside6.qtcore, python3-pyside6.qtgui, python3-pyside6.qtwidgets, procps, iproute2, btrfs-progs, pkexec, hicolor-icon-theme, desktop-file-utils
Recommends: docker.io | docker-ce | docker
Description: system janitor GUI for Parrot OS (runaway killer, ports, snapshots)
 Parrot Janitor is a Qt6 desktop utility that bundles together jobs that htop,
 KDE System Monitor and bleachbit do not do on their own:
 .
  * runaway process detection — flags processes pinned at high CPU for a
    SUSTAINED period (not just momentarily busy), explains what each one is by
    resolving its binary path and Debian package, and kills it behind a
    confirmation dialog with an optional polkit escalation
  * resources — per-thread utilisation bars, a rolling CPU/RAM history chart,
    load average, memory split into in-use / reclaimable cache / free, swap,
    and temperatures read from /sys/class/thermal
  * ports and exposure — classifies every listening socket by scope
    (loopback / LAN / multicast / all interfaces) and verifies whether it is
    actually secured using a real TLS handshake or protocol banner, plus an
    explicit open/closed connect-test of 36 well-known ports and a read-only
    firewall view
  * Docker lab manager (bulk start/stop), btrfs snapshot manager for @ and
    @home, and disk usage / cleanup
 .
 All privileged operations go through polkit (pkexec) rather than plain sudo.
